    <h1>FastAPI <span class="accent">Fundamentals</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">Build high-performance REST APIs with modern Python. Learn FastAPI's core concepts, async features, and automatic documentation generation for production-grade AI services.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="objectives"><h4>Learning Objectives</h4><ul>
    <li>Understand FastAPI's architecture and advantages over traditional frameworks</li>
    <li>Build basic REST endpoints with request/response validation</li>
    <li>Leverage async/await for concurrent request handling</li>
    <li>Implement automatic API documentation and interactive testing</li>
    <li>Configure middleware and error handling</li>
  </ul></div>

  <section class="section" id="intro">
    <h2>What is FastAPI?</h2>
    <p>FastAPI is a modern Python web framework built for building APIs quickly with high performance. Unlike traditional frameworks like Flask or Django, FastAPI leverages Python 3.6+ type hints to provide automatic request validation, serialization, and documentation generation. It's built on Starlette (for the web parts) and Pydantic (for data validation), making it ideal for AI microservices that need to process requests at scale.</p>
    <p>Key advantages for AI practitioners:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Automatic validation</strong>: Pydantic models validate all inputs automatically</li>
      <li><strong>Async by default</strong>: Built-in async/await support for concurrent processing</li>
      <li><strong>Zero boilerplate docs</strong>: Swagger UI and ReDoc auto-generated from code</li>
      <li><strong>High performance</strong>: Comparable to Node.js and Go frameworks</li>
      <li><strong>Type-safe</strong>: Full IDE autocomplete and type checking</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="callout">
      <div class="callout-title">Why FastAPI for AI?</div>
      <p>FastAPI's automatic validation and async support are crucial when building AI services that handle model inference. You can focus on ML logic rather than request parsing and concurrent request management.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="setup">
    <h2>Installation and Basic Setup</h2>
    <p>FastAPI requires Python 3.7+. Install with uvicorn for an async-capable server:</p>
    <div class="code-example"><code><span class="cm"># Install FastAPI and uvicorn (production server)</span>
<span class="kw">pip</span> <span class="va">install</span> <span class="st">'fastapi==0.104.1'</span> <span class="st">'uvicorn[standard]==0.24.0'</span>

<span class="cm"># For async requests and testing</span>
<span class="kw">pip</span> <span class="va">install</span> <span class="st">'httpx==0.25.2'</span> <span class="st">'pytest==7.4.3'</span> <span class="st">'pytest-asyncio==0.21.1'</span></code></div>

    <p>Create your first minimal FastAPI application:</p>
    <div class="code-example"><code><span class="im">from</span> <span class="nm">fastapi</span> <span class="im">import</span> <span class="nm">FastAPI</span>

<span class="nm">app</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">FastAPI</span><span class="op">()</span>

<span class="op">@</span><span class="nm">app</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="fn">get</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="st">"/health"</span><span class="op">)</span>
<span class="kw">async def</span> <span class="fn">health_check</span><span class="op">():</span>
    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="op">{</span><span class="st">"status"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">"healthy"</span><span class="op">}</span></code></div>

    <p>Run with: <code>uvicorn main:app --reload</code></p>
    <p>Visit <code>http://localhost:8000/docs</code> for interactive Swagger UI or <code>http://localhost:8000/redoc</code> for ReDoc documentation.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="routing">
    <h2>Routing and HTTP Methods</h2>
    <p>FastAPI uses Python decorators to define routes. Each decorator corresponds to an HTTP method:</p>
    <div class="code-example"><code><span class="im">from</span> <span class="nm">fastapi</span> <span class="im">import</span> <span class="nm">FastAPI</span>
<span class="im">from</span> <span class="nm">pydantic</span> <span class="im">import</span> <span class="nm">BaseModel</span>

<span class="nm">app</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">FastAPI</span><span class="op">()</span>

<span class="cm"># GET: retrieve data</span>
<span class="op">@</span><span class="nm">app</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="fn">get</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="st">"/predictions/{model_id}"</span><span class="op">)</span>
<span class="kw">async def</span> <span class="fn">get_prediction</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="nm">model_id</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="bi">int</span><span class="op">):</span>
    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="op">{</span><span class="st">"model_id"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="nm">model_id</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="st">"result"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">"prediction_data"</span><span class="op">}</span>

<span class="cm"># POST: create/submit data</span>
<span class="kw">class</span> <span class="nm">PredictionRequest</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="nm">BaseModel</span><span class="op">):</span>
    <span class="nm">text</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="bi">str</span>
    <span class="nm">model_version</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="bi">str</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">"v1"</span>

<span class="op">@</span><span class="nm">app</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="fn">post</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="st">"/predictions"</span><span class="op">)</span>
<span class="kw">async def</span> <span class="fn">create_prediction</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="nm">request</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="nm">PredictionRequest</span><span class="op">):</span>
    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="op">{</span><span class="st">"text"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="nm">request</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">text</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="st">"received"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="kw">True</span><span class="op">}</span>

<span class="cm"># PUT: update existing data</span>
<span class="op">@</span><span class="nm">app</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="fn">put</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="st">"/predictions/{pred_id}"</span><span class="op">)</span>
<span class="kw">async def</span> <span class="fn">update_prediction</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="nm">pred_id</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="bi">int</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="nm">request</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="nm">PredictionRequest</span><span class="op">):</span>
    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="op">{</span><span class="st">"id"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="nm">pred_id</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="st">"updated"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="kw">True</span><span class="op">}</span>

<span class="cm"># DELETE: remove data</span>
<span class="op">@</span><span class="nm">app</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="fn">delete</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="st">"/predictions/{pred_id}"</span><span class="op">)</span>
<span class="kw">async def</span> <span class="fn">delete_prediction</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="nm">pred_id</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="bi">int</span><span class="op">):</span>
    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="op">{</span><span class="st">"id"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="nm">pred_id</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="st">"deleted"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="kw">True</span><span class="op">}</span></code></div>

